"suggestion":"1) Establish clear focal dominance: reduce the 'Kindling' hexagon's visual weight (smaller size, less glow) or reposition it as a clear root node, and increase the 'Skill Codex' title's prominence to anchor the top. 2) Group the three branches explicitly: add subtle background tints or vertical dividers behind each column, and label each branch at the top (e.g., 'Ember Path', 'Ashen Path', 'Radiance Path') to create immediate visual grouping. 3) Strengthen connection lines: increase their thickness and contrast, and add directional arrows or gradient fades to make parent-child relationships immediately readable. 4) Reduce badge noise: make the '1' cost badges smaller and lower-contrast, or move them to a tooltip on hover, so the node states (Mastered/Learned/Unlocked/Locked) become the primary visual signal. 5) Move the legend closer to the tree or integrate it as a compact inline key near the top of the tree area. 6) Simplify the sidebar: collapse the 'Disciplines' section into a compact summary or move it below the fold, so the skill-point card and level/XP remain the primary sidebar information without competing with the tree."
}

